-- title:
--   Proposition 3 — full traversal attains expected cost $\mu(a,d)$ per target observation
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a rule that traverses full episodes without voluntary aborts and decides when to stop from the target outcomes seen so far (any such stopping decision), at depth $d\ge0$ with survival $a\in(0,1]$, with any side law, and let $q\in[0,1]$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_qC=\mu(a,d)\,\mathbb E_qN ,
--   $$
--
--   in $[0,\infty]$. A full episode costs $1+\sum_{j=0}^d a^j$ in expectation and reaches the target with probability $a^d$, and whether the next target observation is requested depends only on earlier target outcomes. Applied to the SPRT, this gives $\mathbb E_qC=\mu(a,d)\,\mathbb E_q\tau$, so the multiplier of Proposition 3's lower bound is attained.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: "Traversing episodes without voluntary aborts" (an informal class of rules) → fullTraversalRule W stopDec for any stopping decision stopDec on the list of target outcomes seen so far; reason: the source does not define the class; this reading matches the proof's "whether observation i is requested depends only on earlier target outcomes" and contains the SPRT, the rule the proof applies it to
--   - encoding: navigation and target outcomes with their stated conditional laws given the history; old transcript generated by a common kernel under all compared parameters; private randomness → side variable w ∼ ν (old data and private randomness, law free of q), independent of an i.i.d. Bernoulli(a) navigation tape and an i.i.d. Bernoulli(q) target tape; the k-th navigation attempt reads navigation entry k, the j-th target attempt reads target entry j (lawQ); reason: attempts are predictable, so each reads a fresh entry independent of everything observed; the joint law of (old data, randomness, fresh history) is the source's
--   - encoding: C the new physical cost (root setups, navigation attempts, target attempts), N the number of target observations, expectations E_q → cost and targetCount valued in ℕ∞, expectations as lintegrals in ℝ≥0∞ (expCost, expTargets); reason: same quantities; a rule that never stops has cost ⊤ and never accepts
--   - encoding: an auditor may adaptively abort or restart; root resets allowed, internal resets not → actions setup / attempt / accept / stop; setup issued during an episode abandons it; attempt with no active episode acts as a root setup (cost 1); decisions are measurable in w for each fresh history; reason: every abort/restart is a root setup; no action yields a free observation; measurability makes the acceptance events and costs well defined
-- source:
--   Q. Li, When Can Physical Evidence Survive a World-Model Update? Finite-cost re-auditing and reusable policy certificates, review revision of 3 November 2026 (STOC 2027 submission, sha256 a20c437b34115b84982339e9a6fa319cb3a66f66d9d4c474465cbb954c79093d), Proposition 3 (The physical navigation multiplier), second sentence, p.3 (PDF p.4); used in the proof of Theorem 4, p.4: "summing conditional expectations gives EqC = µ(a, d)Eqτ"

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LimitedPriceChanges_LowerBound_KL
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_mu
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_Delta
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_Rule
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_run
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_lawQ
import Definitions.Def_PhysReaudit_fullTraversalRule

open MeasureTheory

namespace PhysReaudit

/-- **Proposition 3, second sentence** (Q. Li, *When Can Physical Evidence Survive a World-Model Update?*, review revision of 3 November 2026 (sha256 a20c437b…), Proposition 3, p.3 (PDF p.4)): "Traversing episodes without
voluntary aborts attains expected cost µ(a, d) per target observation."

For every rule that traverses full episodes and decides to stop only from the target outcomes seen so far
(`fullTraversalRule W stopDec`, any `stopDec`), every side law `ν`, `a ∈ (0, 1]`, depth `d` and
`q ∈ [0, 1]`: `E_q C = µ(a, d) · E_q N`, in `ℝ≥0∞`. -/
theorem proposition_3_attain {W : Type} [MeasurableSpace W] (ν : Measure W) [IsProbabilityMeasure ν]
    (stopDec : List Bool → Option Bool) {a : ℝ} {d : ℕ} (ha : 0 < a) (ha1 : a ≤ 1) {q : ℝ}
    (hq : q ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) :
    expCost (fullTraversalRule W stopDec) ν a d q
      = ENNReal.ofReal (mu a d) * expTargets (fullTraversalRule W stopDec) ν a d q := by sorry

end PhysReaudit
